  nonce: '1437'  # 1437
  data:  # 1437
    kind: work_item  # 1437
    title: "PHASE 2 (gated on v9/v10): migrate module-slot violators — objc receiver-variable, cpp include disjunction, sentinels — per ADR-0024 step 7"  # 1437
    status: todo_hard  # 1437
    priority: 3  # 1437
    parent:  # 1437
    tags:  # 1437
    - axis  # 1437
    - io_boundary  # 1437
    - architecture  # 1437
    isbefore: []  # 1437
    duplicate_of: []  # 1437
    not_duplicate_of: []  # 1437
    pr_ref:  # 1437
    description: "PHASE 2 of the owner's 2026-09-01 ruling (a) on WI-livar: ADR-0024 step 7,\n\"migrate violators\". GATED -- do not start this before the gate clears.\n\nWHY IT IS GATED, stated so the next reader does not re-derive it. external_symbol\nnode ids EMBED the module slot (rust:external:0-0:File::open), so changing what an\nanalyzer puts in that slot changes emitted ids. WI-talos DECISION 3 already\nallocates v9 (relabel only, digest-compatible with v8) and v10 (the bitbake/bibtex\nstable_id fix, no compatibility declared), and the scheme bumps are gated behind\ntwo releases. A third content-changing bump queues behind those. ADR-0024's own\nworkflow draws this line -- steps 1-4 mandatory and additive, step 7 explicitly\noptional and separate -- which is why the axis DECLARATION ships now and this does\nnot.\n\nWHAT MIGRATES, from the module-key concept audit (65,187 external refs, 21-repo\n10-language cold cohort; write-up\n~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/concept-audit-module-key_09012026.md):\n\n  * OBJECTIVE-C writes module_path=receiver_name LITERALLY. 1,102 of 4,207 refs\n    (26%) on the objc+swift repos carry a local identifier -- expectation,\n    request, session, resp, download, components. This is the largest violator\n    and the least ambiguous: a receiver variable is not a module under any\n    reading of the axiom.\n  * DISJUNCTIONS, 6.2%. cpp joins every #include in the file into one\n    comma-separated slot. It is a SET, and the analyzer says so itself. Whether\n    the axiom admits a disjunction as a legal value or the shape moves to a\n    sibling field is the ADR's call, NOT this item's to assume.\n  * SENTINELS: 'external' (1.5%) and bash's 'redirect' (0.1%, whose name slot is\n    '>' -- not a call at all).\n\n  NOT violators, and do not migrate them: relative paths (2.7%, a legitimate\n  module id in JS/TS) and C/C++ header names like <string.h> (1.4%). An earlier\n  cut of this audit bucketed by a leading '<' and swept 929 legitimate headers\n  into \"sentinel\", inflating the non-identity share from 7.8% to 11.9%. The\n  corrected number is 7.8%.\n\nFIRST STEP WHEN UNGATED: re-measure. These are 2026-09-01 figures and the\nanalyzers will have moved. Follow ADR-0023's four-phase migration shape --\nconsumers, producers, schema bump, deprecation removal -- not a single sweeping\nproducer rewrite."  # 1437
    fields: {}  # 1437
- op: discuss  # cd1c
  at: '2026-09-01T20:13:59Z'  # cd1c
  by: agent  # cd1c
  actor: jgstern_agent  # cd1c
  clock: 2  # cd1c
  nonce: cd1c  # cd1c
  message: "CORRECTION BEFORE ANY ROW MOVES: this item's objc bullet is mis-aimed as filed. objc.py:644 does write module_path=receiver_name, but the site is GATED on receiver_name[0].isupper() (:637), and a capitalised Objective-C message receiver is normally a CLASS name -- so objc's slot is predominantly a TYPE, which is axiom-conformant, not a receiver variable. The lowercase identifiers the audit counted (expectation, request, session, resp, download, components) cannot come from that site. The receiver-VARIABLE notion is SWIFT's: swift.py:1223 falls back receiver_type -> import alias -> receiver_hint -> 'external', and the third clause is the violator. The audit's '1,102 of 4,207 (26%)' was over the COMBINED objc+swift cohort and must be re-derived per-language before this item's population is sized. Full trace on INV-kotob."  # cd1c
- op: discuss  # 7d28
  at: '2026-10-01T12:52:18Z'  # 7d28
  by: agent  # 7d28
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 7d28
  clock: 3  # 7d28
  nonce: 7d28  # 7d28
  message: "From WI-dason-bijot-punop-kosud-nifuz-fusuh-jibof-dajik (branch jgstern-agent/fix/dason, local, not merged): objc.py carried a comment saying a PROJECT class in the class-message module slot was \"WI-marok's question\". WI-dason answered it in the analyzer instead: a class message to a class the repo declares now leaves the slot at the external sentinel and carries the class in receiver_type_hint (583 of 3300 typed slots on the four-repo objc corpus; 3500 of 14792 on seven), and __auto_type / instancetype / a misparsed nonnull no longer reach the slot (111 + 13). This CHANGES emitted external_symbol ids (objc:Svc:0-0:alloc -> objc:external:0-0:alloc), with no stable_id scheme bump -- the same thing WI-higob and INV-kotob did when they moved objc/swift slot content. If the v9/v10 gate in this item's description is meant to cover analyzer-level slot corrections like these, the integrator should know before merging WI-dason. The objc bullet in this item (receiver VARIABLE) was already corrected on 2026-09-01; after WI-dason the objc class-message site writes only an external class or nothing."  # 7d28
